window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>She thought she was safe.</p> <p>She thought he was hers.</p> <p>But nothing stays innocent forever—not in Holt Manor.</p> <p>In the second installment of The Wallflower, Daisy is no longer just the quiet girl in the shadows. She’s at the center of a world she doesn’t yet understand, surrounded by secrets she was never meant to uncover. As her relationship with Marcus deepens, so does her entanglement with the Holt family—and the dark legacy that lives behind the Left-Wing doors. There are games being played. Rules being rewritten. And Daisy is starting to wonder if the man in her bed is really the one holding the reins. </p> <p>Tense, erotic, and psychologically immersive, The Wallflower – Book Two is a descent into power, possession, and the spiral of surrender. The house is watching. The walls are listening. And the truth is getting harder to ignore.</p>"; 
